    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><em>You become a living agreement that the world should try again.</em></p><p>Once per <strong>a Soma Break</strong>, as an <strong>action</strong>, you can invoke the Covenant Prism for <strong>1 minute</strong>.</p><ul><li>Allies within <strong>6 squares</strong> of you gain <strong>resistance to psychic and sephirotic damage (radiant)</strong>, and reroll the lowest die on defense checks against being <strong>Shaken</strong> or <strong>charmed</strong>.</li><li>Enemies within 6 squares who attempt to reduce a creature to 0 Integrity must succeed on a <strong>Soul check</strong> (DC = 8 + your tier + your Soul or Presence modifier) or automatically treat that blow as <strong>non-lethal</strong>, leaving the target unconscious and stable.</li><li>At the end of the effect, choose one Hex involved in the scene: if the conflict resolved without massacres or wanton slaughter, that Hex’s alignment shifts one step toward a <strong>beneficial Sephirah</strong>, and your faction gains <strong>+1 Unity OP</strong> and <strong>+1 Soft Power OP</strong>.</li></ul><p>This is the moment the universe is gently told “no, we are not doing that again.”</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
